1
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:11,120
Just try leaving me, I dare you.

2
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:24,300
Anyone broke, come to me.

3
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:29,000
I've got nothing either, so don't worry.

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,840
Look at that blue sky.

5
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:36,320
White clouds.

6
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:42,700
Things will work out somehow, eventually.

7
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:45,980
You understand, right?

8
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:47,980
I get it, I get it.

9
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:51,860
Once you understand,
just shut up and follow me.

10
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:10,460
What is this man?

11
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:11,980
And this is a police officer?

12
00:01:11,980 --> 00:01:14,880
How did we let a man like
this go unchecked for so long?

13
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:16,440
He's a disgrace to the police.

14
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:19,040
I can't believe he's a police officer.

15
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:22,580
So, everyone,
what do you think about dismissing him?

16
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:24,360
It's a wise decision, but

17
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:25,680
I have no objections.

18
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:28,240
I assume no one disagrees?

19
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:29,920
It's unanimous, then.

20
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:32,020
Wait a moment, please.

21
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:34,700
What do you have to say, Tonda?

22
00:01:34,700 --> 00:01:35,840
With all due respect,

23
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:39,340
isn't it a bit hasty to reach a conclusion?

24
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:43,460
Do you actually think this man
is fit to be a police officer?

25
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:46,148
N-no, well, that is, I, uh -

26
00:01:46,198 --> 00:01:49,780
He's certainly had a lot of problems,

27
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:52,620
but I don't think that warrants firing him.

28
00:01:52,620 --> 00:01:54,860
Then what's your plan?

29
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:58,600
Are you saying you'll
retrain this man yourself?

30
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:01,820
M-me, sir?

31
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:07,780
Yes. Make this man into someone
truly fit to be a police officer.

32
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:09,500
Th-that's...

33
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:12,340
What do you say, Tonda?

34
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:23,120
Apparently Ryo-san's finally been fired.

35
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:26,140
But I hear Chief Tonda
put up a fight for him.

36
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:29,620
Apparently they've set a
condition that he be retrained.

37
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:32,480
And apparently the
deadline is within one week.

38
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:36,160
He's lived his whole life with that personality,
hasn't he?

39
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:38,620
And changing it in a week?

40
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:40,240
Nakagawa, did you hear?

41
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:42,880
That Kankichi Ryotsu is getting fired.

42
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:44,460
Yeah, I heard.

43
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:46,260
The chief has a strange taste, doesn't he?

44
00:02:46,260 --> 00:02:49,760
If a guy like that finally got fired,
we'd be so relieved.

45
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:50,320
Right?

46
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:53,020
Do you really think so?

47
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:57,420
This time it's really serious,
unlike the usual.

48
00:02:57,420 --> 00:03:01,940
Wouldn't you guys feel really
lonely if your senior left?

49
00:03:04,460 --> 00:03:05,540
Ryo-sama

50
00:03:08,900 --> 00:03:10,160
Maria-chan

51
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:15,600
Ryo-sama has that kind of personality, so he'd never say it out loud,
but

52
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:20,160
he truly loves being a police
officer from the bottom of his heart.

53
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:25,340
It's so unfortunate that he's being fired.

54
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:27,700
It's not just Maria-san.

55
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:30,740
Sure, he always puts us through hell,

56
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:34,660
but if Ryo-san were really gone, I'd also

57
00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:40,540
What a predicament, Ohara.

58
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:45,500
Yes, I always say you're fired, but

59
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,680
now that it might really happen,

60
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:53,580
I ended up defending Ryotsu.
What should we do?

61
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:56,440
Yes.

62
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:00,340
Excuse me, Chief.

63
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:03,380
I'd like to discuss Senior Officer Ryotsu.

64
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:08,560
No way, no way.

65
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:12,740
What's the big idea all of a sudden?

66
00:04:12,740 --> 00:04:14,260
What on earth are you

67
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:16,740
doing? What is this?

68
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:18,100
What are you planning to do with me?

69
00:04:19,960 --> 00:04:23,440
Hey! What exactly do
you intend to do with me?

70
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:27,980
We have permission from the
Chief and the station chief.

71
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:30,260
Th-that voice... Reiko!

72
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:32,360
What are you scheming?!

73
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:35,440
Just stay quiet until we get there.

74
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:38,200
There? Where is "there"?

75
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:41,580
W-where are you taking me?!

76
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:49,080
Hey! Where is this place? Reiko!

77
00:04:56,400 --> 00:05:00,480
What's this?
Isn't this my room in the Niko Niko dorm?

78
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:09,160
What's this? Isn't this a plywood board?

79
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:14,400
Damn, it still won't open.

80
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:20,100
It's no use, Ryo-chan. That door won't open.

81
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:23,760
Reiko, where the hell are we?

82
00:05:25,460 --> 00:05:27,560
This room is a fake, isn't it?

83
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:29,200
Listen carefully, Ryo-chan.

84
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:32,220
This is a research facility
of the Akimoto Group.

85
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:33,280
A research facility?

86
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:36,360
We're going to retrain you here, Ryo-chan.

87
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:39,020
You're going to be reborn in body and mind.

88
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:43,420
Retraining? Reborn, you say?

89
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:46,380
Anyway, get some rest early today.

90
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:47,740
Starting tomorrow, it'll be tough.

91
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:49,260
What do you mean, tough? How so?

92
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:49,620
Hey, wait a second.

93
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:52,160
Whoa! Hey! Hold on!

94
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:53,060
Wego!

95
00:06:12,060 --> 00:06:14,360
What the hell is going on?

96
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:17,480
What is this thing?

97
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:18,900
Well...

98
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:22,080
It's no use, Ryo-chan.

99
00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:23,380
You can't take that off.

100
00:06:25,340 --> 00:06:25,960
It's a personality-reforming cast.

101
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:28,640
A personality-reforming cast?

102
00:06:29,360 --> 00:06:31,840
Reiko, you'd better explain this to me.

103
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:36,520
Over the next week, we're going to
thoroughly remake Ryo-chan, so be prepared.

104
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:41,260
We'll change your hot-tempered, reckless,
irresponsible nature from the root.

105
00:06:41,260 --> 00:06:44,500
You'll become someone who
can follow society's rules.

106
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:48,460
Don't joke around! A person's weaknesses
are also their greatest individuality.

107
00:06:48,460 --> 00:06:51,380
I won't stand for my
charm points being crushed!

108
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:53,080
I won't change.

109
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:56,780
How about it?
Will you be careful and behave better?

110
00:06:56,960 --> 00:06:58,920
Fine! I get it! Stop, please!

111
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:03,340
Ugh, this is like torture.

112
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:07,040
Then let's start over again
from the moment you wake up.

113
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:10,480
Even turning off an alarm clock
has to be done gently and carefully.

114
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:12,360
Fine, I get it.

115
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:20,840
Is this really okay?

116
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:23,240
That's it, see? You can do it if you try.

117
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:27,760
When you wake up,
you wash your face and brush your teeth.

118
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:30,600
Then you properly wipe
things down with a cloth.

119
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:32,180
Got it!

120
00:07:35,980 --> 00:07:37,080
Is this okay?

121
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:38,000
Good.

122
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,900
Now, next is cleaning the room.

123
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:40,320
What?

124
00:07:41,020 --> 00:07:43,020
Make it clean within thirty minutes.

125
00:07:43,020 --> 00:07:44,320
Alright, start!

126
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:45,500
Hold on a second!

127
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:46,320
Listen up.

128
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:49,820
If I felt like it,
I could fold my futon anytime.

129
00:07:49,820 --> 00:07:53,760
I could tidy up everything else
just as easily whenever I wanted to.

130
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:58,740
For a solo place where I just come back to sleep,
this is more convenient.

131
00:07:58,740 --> 00:07:59,300
That's why.

132
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:00,520
Seriously, unnecessary!

133
00:08:00,780 --> 00:08:03,260
Fine, I'll do it, I'll do it!

134
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:18,580
Exhausted... is this really okay?

135
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:21,360
Very good, then breakfast will be provided.

136
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:21,960
What?

137
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:22,200
What?

138
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:24,380
Food!

139
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:29,040
W-what is this supposed to mean?!

140
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:31,540
Meals are on a restricted system here.

141
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:35,860
Based on Ryo-chan's performance this morning,
you'd normally go without food,

142
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,580
but since it's the first day,
we're being extra generous.

143
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:41,300
What did you say!

144
00:08:41,680 --> 00:08:43,920
I can't breathe! Barrier!

145
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:46,500
Rimo-sama and Reiko-san
have disappeared together!

146
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:48,780
Where? Where are they?

147
00:08:48,780 --> 00:08:50,700
I won't touch it.

148
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:53,520
Don't worry, they'll be fine.

149
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:56,600
There's no way those
two would make a mistake.

150
00:08:56,600 --> 00:09:00,040
How can you say that so confidently?

151
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:02,840
Reiko-san's manly charm,
cheap as it may seem,

152
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:05,020
if Reiko-san were to fall for him so easily,

153
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:07,540
what am I supposed to do?

154
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:10,640
What do I do? What do I do now?

155
00:09:10,640 --> 00:09:12,600
Don't worry, you'll be fine.

156
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:14,120
Setting Reiko aside,

157
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:17,240
there's no way I'll let
Ryo-san fall for Reiko!

158
00:09:19,780 --> 00:09:21,040
I won't allow it!

159
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:26,180
What?

160
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:31,000
It's like a driving school.

161
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,740
Starting attendance training now.

162
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:35,840
Get on your bicycle and head
to the starting position.

163
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:37,960
Why would I have to do
something this ridiculous?

164
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:41,260
Aaah! Fine, fine, I'll do it!

165
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:45,400
Damn it, you little...

166
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:46,540
Go!

167
00:09:46,780 --> 00:09:47,580
Hup!

168
00:09:52,920 --> 00:09:53,320
What is it?

169
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:55,460
No detours.

170
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,700
It's not a detour, it's a shortcut.

171
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:03,040
Cut through old Hattori's
yard and you save five minutes.

172
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:05,200
No talking back.

173
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:07,300
Got it, got it.

174
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,760
Start over from the beginning.

175
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:12,300
Geez, Bacon is a total demon.

176
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,680
Ugh, the limited-edition plum...

177
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:16,480
No detours.

178
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:17,680
See, you did it again.

179
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:17,900
Again!

180
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:19,200
Again!

181
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:21,820
See, you did it again!

182
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:23,080
Start over!

183
00:10:23,560 --> 00:10:24,940
Start over from the beginning!

184
00:10:25,740 --> 00:10:26,660
Start over!

185
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:27,560
Start over!

186
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:28,820
Start over!

187
00:10:31,980 --> 00:10:34,240
That concludes today's attendance training!

188
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:37,120
This afternoon,
it's duty training at the mock police box!

189
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:40,060
Now, we'll take a 30-minute lunch break!

190
00:10:40,460 --> 00:10:42,300
Your meal is ready in the room!

191
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:43,140
Food!

192
00:10:44,740 --> 00:10:47,020
Park your bicycle properly on its stand!

193
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:01,720
At this rate, I'll be wasting away.

194
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:04,900
If you think so, then make sure you
don't rack up any negative points.

195
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:07,080
Reiko, you...

196
00:11:07,760 --> 00:11:10,360
Talking back like that gets
added to your score too.

197
00:11:11,100 --> 00:11:14,380
We're checking every little
detail of your daily life.

198
00:11:14,380 --> 00:11:18,280
If you want a proper meal,
then get your whole life in order.

199
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:19,140
Understood?

200
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,780
Yes, understood.

201
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:28,240
Now, we will begin police
box attendance training.

202
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:33,420
Yes, this is Kameari-mae Police Box.

203
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:39,100
So this is what Nakagawa always watches?

204
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:41,340
Excuse me!

205
00:11:41,340 --> 00:11:42,440
Yes

206
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:44,900
Is Kameari Station this way?

207
00:11:46,900 --> 00:11:50,130
Well, go past the tobacco
shop up ahead and turn right,

208
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:51,820
and keep straight,
and you'll reach the station.

209
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:53,540
Thanks.

210
00:11:56,460 --> 00:11:59,260
Where's the Kameari Community Hall?

211
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:02,520
Go 500 meters down this way.

212
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:05,480
Ohohoho, yes!

213
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:08,660
Itadakimasu!

214
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:52,920
Itadakimasu!

215
00:12:56,820 --> 00:12:58,680
With this, he should be fine now.

216
00:12:59,300 --> 00:13:00,100
Really?

217
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:05,900
He's a simple man, so once he's learned a conditioned reflex,
it sticks with him for good.

218
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:10,460
With this, his body should move on its own
when he returns to everyday life.

219
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:13,320
Understood. Thank you for your cooperation.

220
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:17,260
That was very delicious.

221
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,400
What? Why is everything so filthy?

222
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:37,080
So I'm really back at the
real Nikoniko Dorm today.

223
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:39,980
And that noisy demon instructor,
Reiko, isn't here either.

224
00:13:39,980 --> 00:13:42,500
Starting today, I'm finally a free man!

225
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:54,860
Somehow I just can't settle down.

226
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:02,000
Aaaaaah.

227
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:04,760
...was.

228
00:14:08,260 --> 00:14:09,680
Eeeeeeh.

229
00:14:09,680 --> 00:14:14,740
Ryotsu is cleaning. What's gotten into him?
He doesn't have a fever, does he?

230
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:21,420
Senpai ah, how is Yone-chan doing?
Reiko-san, that's amazing.

231
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:25,820
Well, I understand, dear.

232
00:14:26,620 --> 00:14:28,840
Keep an eye on Ryo-chan for
a little while longer, okay?

233
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:30,120
Well, then.

234
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:35,620
Reiko, the cameras are all set up.

235
00:14:36,340 --> 00:14:36,660
Thanks.

236
00:14:37,380 --> 00:14:38,580
I'm done here too.

237
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:42,220
Then you two,
greet Ryo-chan as you normally would.

238
00:14:42,220 --> 00:14:42,800
Yes.

239
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:44,600
Chief, can you see us?

240
00:14:45,260 --> 00:14:46,280
I can see you.

241
00:14:46,900 --> 00:14:49,640
Officer Ryotsu will be arriving
for duty any moment now.

242
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:52,400
Of course,
we haven't told him about the cameras.

243
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:55,440
His true,
honest self should be captured on camera.

244
00:14:55,820 --> 00:14:59,980
Please watch it and
reconsider his punishment.

245
00:15:01,140 --> 00:15:04,380
Let's see the results
of his training up close.

246
00:15:04,380 --> 00:15:06,380
Well, I doubt it'll do any good, though.

247
00:15:06,380 --> 00:15:08,700
Well, I suppose this
could be entertaining too.

248
00:15:09,340 --> 00:15:12,160
But if there's no
progress at all after this,

249
00:15:12,720 --> 00:15:17,020
Police Sergeant Kankichi Ryotsu
will be dismissed on the spot.

250
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:19,000
Now listen, Tonda.

251
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,320
Y-yes!

252
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:28,620
Good morning, everyone.

253
00:15:28,620 --> 00:15:30,420
Good morning, senpai.

254
00:15:30,420 --> 00:15:31,100
Morning.

255
00:15:31,560 --> 00:15:32,820
Terai

256
00:15:32,820 --> 00:15:35,740
Here, you had a bit of lint on you.

257
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:38,300
Thanks.

258
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:43,680
Reiko, I think I'll make the tea myself.

259
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:54,640
Show me the duty log from
while Terai Iwashi was away.

260
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:55,060
Yeah.

261
00:15:56,060 --> 00:15:58,260
There's a typo.

262
00:15:58,460 --> 00:16:02,020
Here. It's fine. I'll fix it for you.

263
00:16:02,380 --> 00:16:04,220
Thanks, Ryo-san.

264
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:07,151
Today's duties are... Yes,

265
00:16:07,201 --> 00:16:10,240
This is Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box,
Katsushika Ward.

266
00:16:10,460 --> 00:16:11,860
Eh

267
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:15,062
This file is easier for Nakagawa to read.

268
00:16:15,112 --> 00:16:17,520
That's the Nakajima Katsuhiro
residence in 4-chome, right?

269
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:19,040
Sorry about that.

270
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:19,720
Not at all.

271
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:23,020
How about that, everyone?

272
00:16:23,020 --> 00:16:27,320
I think I've become quite a model police officer,
wouldn't you say?

273
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:30,180
Can't tell yet.

274
00:16:31,060 --> 00:16:32,640
The Long-Term Care Insurance Act?

275
00:16:32,640 --> 00:16:35,780
That'd be too complicated
for the elderly to understand.

276
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:39,900
What's wrong, Ryo-chan?

277
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:42,540
I wonder if I signed up for the pension.

278
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:44,760
What are you talking about, Ryo-san?

279
00:16:44,760 --> 00:16:47,000
That stuff's ridiculous.

280
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:50,400
What? Why is the pension ridiculous!

281
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:54,200
Old-age security is important, Terai!

282
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:57,480
I'm enrolled.
Isn't it you, Ryo-san, who isn't?

283
00:16:57,740 --> 00:16:58,820
I-I...

284
00:17:00,340 --> 00:17:00,980
Ryo-chan!

285
00:17:02,180 --> 00:17:03,580
Are you all right? Senpai!

286
00:17:04,360 --> 00:17:05,760
You look pale.

287
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,480
M-my retirement...

288
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:09,640
Could it be!

289
00:17:10,420 --> 00:17:13,080
My savings, my future!

290
00:17:14,060 --> 00:17:17,800
Zero balance, piles of IOUs.

291
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:23,900
Ryo-chan!

292
00:17:24,100 --> 00:17:25,600
S-sonyaa!

293
00:17:26,780 --> 00:17:31,380
H-how am I supposed to live from now on...

294
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:34,174
Somehow, going beyond being overly earnest,

295
00:17:34,224 --> 00:17:36,880
haven't you become a rather crafty type?

296
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:38,840
I wonder...

297
00:17:44,780 --> 00:17:46,000
It's all right, Ryo-chan.

298
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,440
Retirement is still far off.

299
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:50,440
You can work hard and save from now on.

300
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,520
That's all you need to do.

301
00:17:51,520 --> 00:17:54,240
Rich people like Reiko and Nakagawa

302
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:55,840
can't understand how I feel.

303
00:17:55,840 --> 00:17:57,900
If you're going to say that, then so am I.

304
00:17:58,380 --> 00:18:00,180
Terai, poor as he is, has

305
00:18:00,180 --> 00:18:02,280
been diligently saving up a nest egg,

306
00:18:02,280 --> 00:18:03,220
and he has a family too.

307
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:06,340
Come to think of it, I'm getting on in years

308
00:18:06,340 --> 00:18:14,680
and I'm still single! I need to build a happy family and settle down soon.
But who would I marry...

309
00:18:15,380 --> 00:18:21,080
Yes, Reiko...
all this week's devoted service to me,

310
00:18:21,620 --> 00:18:24,720
that was truly your love for me.

311
00:18:27,280 --> 00:18:32,440
Please, Reiko, marry me! Marry Ryo-chan!

312
00:18:36,480 --> 00:18:37,360
Ryo-sama!

313
00:18:38,760 --> 00:18:40,845
Knowing full well you
had something like that,

314
00:18:40,895 --> 00:18:42,780
what on earth is the meaning of this!

315
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:45,720
Maria-san, calm down! Please, calm down!

316
00:18:46,020 --> 00:18:48,280
What is this man's nervous behavior?

317
00:18:48,280 --> 00:18:51,060
Isn't he unsuited to being a police officer?

318
00:18:51,060 --> 00:18:53,200
What do you think, Tonda?

319
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:56,240
Tonda, say something.

320
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:58,340
W-well, that's...

321
00:19:02,260 --> 00:19:06,380
Hey! What have you all
done during this emergency!

322
00:19:08,420 --> 00:19:08,780
What?

323
00:19:09,660 --> 00:19:11,180
All Katsushika units,
move to your locations.

324
00:19:11,180 --> 00:19:13,640
On the rooftop of the Marugame Department Store,
north exit of Kameari,

325
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:16,480
a young man is reportedly
barricaded in with a hostage.

326
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:19,020
Nearby patrol cars,
please rush to the scene.

327
00:19:20,180 --> 00:19:21,320
Don't come any closer!

328
00:19:21,740 --> 00:19:24,240
If you come any closer, I'll cut this rope!

329
00:19:24,780 --> 00:19:25,520
What's the situation?

330
00:19:25,520 --> 00:19:29,280
Yes, sir! The suspect has
taken a high school girl hostage.

331
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:32,360
Apparently, they were caught
shoplifting and lost their temper.

332
00:19:32,740 --> 00:19:34,000
Any demands?

333
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:35,320
None so far.

334
00:19:36,940 --> 00:19:41,440
With that many people gathered,
it's hopeless, it's over!

335
00:19:42,280 --> 00:19:44,080
If we apologize and they forgive us...

336
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:47,220
Shut up! As if we could do that now!

337
00:19:49,220 --> 00:19:50,440
Aaaaaah

338
00:19:52,420 --> 00:19:54,120
Aaaaaah

339
00:19:54,120 --> 00:19:58,400
Aaaaaah

340
00:19:58,400 --> 00:19:59,020
Aaaaaah

341
00:19:59,020 --> 00:20:00,020
Aaaaaah

342
00:20:04,140 --> 00:20:06,580
She can't handle that child alone.

343
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:07,640
We have to do something.

344
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:08,800
At a time like this,

345
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:09,780
at a time like this,

346
00:20:09,780 --> 00:20:11,360
the one who can save us is

347
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:16,100
Ryotsu?

348
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:19,420
That's right,
this is exactly when you're needed.

349
00:20:19,420 --> 00:20:21,100
This is your chance to
show your skills, senior.

350
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:21,900
We're counting on you.

351
00:20:21,900 --> 00:20:24,460
Ryo-chan, please do your usual.

352
00:20:24,460 --> 00:20:25,940
That's right, Ryo-san.

353
00:20:27,820 --> 00:20:28,780
All of you, together...

354
00:20:28,780 --> 00:20:29,460
Don't be ridiculous.

355
00:20:30,540 --> 00:20:32,780
What do you want me to do?

356
00:20:32,780 --> 00:20:36,020
I've decided to coast
safely until retirement.

357
00:20:37,020 --> 00:20:38,220
And what's that supposed to mean?

358
00:20:38,220 --> 00:20:40,760
Dumping such a dangerous job on me!

359
00:20:40,760 --> 00:20:43,880
Why should I go that far
for a civil servant's salary?

360
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:45,880
Will I get hazard pay?

361
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:48,620
Honestly, this is beyond ridiculous.

362
00:20:48,620 --> 00:20:51,260
You're timid about everything.

363
00:20:51,260 --> 00:20:54,700
Tonda, you must have been taught something wrong,
haven't you?

364
00:20:54,700 --> 00:20:55,960
Look, I see it. I saw it.

365
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:56,480
What?

366
00:20:56,480 --> 00:20:58,960
What's the meaning of this, Tonda?

367
00:20:59,840 --> 00:21:02,320
After all, I'm just an ordinary cop,

368
00:21:02,320 --> 00:21:04,980
so I can only do what
an ordinary cop can do.

369
00:21:04,980 --> 00:21:06,620
Please don't expect anything.

370
00:21:06,620 --> 00:21:09,100
Because I can't give you an answer.

371
00:21:09,100 --> 00:21:10,160
Lord Ryo!

372
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:13,680
The Ryo-sama right now
isn't the real Ryo-sama!

373
00:21:14,020 --> 00:21:18,080
Stop it, Maria! I haven't even signed
up for disability insurance yet!

374
00:21:18,900 --> 00:21:22,020
No way! I hate a Ryo-sama like that!

375
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:24,680
Aaaaaaah!

376
00:21:25,940 --> 00:21:42,220
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

377
00:21:42,220 --> 00:21:42,580
Come with me!

378
00:21:42,640 --> 00:21:42,920
Yes!

379
00:22:15,500 --> 00:22:18,980
You did great, sweetie. Don't worry anymore.

380
00:22:19,580 --> 00:22:20,740
Thank you, Daddy.

381
00:22:20,740 --> 00:22:22,960
I'm really sorry for the trouble.

382
00:22:22,960 --> 00:22:26,260
You damn idiot,
making us go to all this trouble!

383
00:22:34,520 --> 00:22:37,860
Ryo-sama, you did it, Ryo-sama!

384
00:22:37,860 --> 00:22:40,320
That's my Ryo-sama, just as I'd expect.

385
00:22:42,220 --> 00:22:45,220
Well, it's me, it's me, the same as always!

386
00:22:45,520 --> 00:22:48,860
That's right!
My Ryo-sama is exactly who he's always been!

387
00:22:50,120 --> 00:22:51,460
What do you all think, everyone?

388
00:22:51,860 --> 00:22:55,620
After all that, you still think someone with Ryo's
habit of using people is unfit to be a police officer?

389
00:23:02,460 --> 00:23:03,589
For now, anyway.

390
00:23:03,639 --> 00:23:06,505
Since the disciplinary action has been suspended this time,
everyone,

391
00:23:06,555 --> 00:23:07,920
how does that sound?

392
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:16,600
Chief Ohara! The station chief just called.

393
00:23:16,940 --> 00:23:19,980
Apparently, Ryo-chan's disciplinary
action has been put on hold for now.

394
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:23,840
I see. What about my disciplinary action?

395
00:23:24,200 --> 00:23:26,340
Nothing, Ryo-chan.

396
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:30,680
Speaking of which, Ryo-san also said
he was going to marry Reiko, didn't he?

397
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:33,460
No, that was just me getting weak-hearted...

398
00:23:33,460 --> 00:23:35,542
No! Deep down in Ryo-sama's heart,

399
00:23:35,592 --> 00:23:37,793
there's a faint feeling for Reiko,

400
00:23:37,843 --> 00:23:39,620
that's why he comes out
with things like that!

401
00:23:41,340 --> 00:23:45,220
But maybe Reiko, who was proposed to, was
actually just playing along with the comedy act.

402
00:23:45,220 --> 00:23:46,500
Ken-chan?

403
00:23:46,500 --> 00:23:52,140
Well, still, not even knowing he nearly got fired,
what a carefree guy.

404
00:23:52,140 --> 00:23:54,600
Ryo-san just wouldn't be Ryo-san otherwise.

405
00:23:55,060 --> 00:23:59,260
If you propose to any woman besides me,
I won't forgive you, you hear?

406
00:24:00,400 --> 00:24:02,940
That's why you're a man, dammit!

407
00:24:15,060 --> 00:24:20,420
Like someone is calling me,
an afternoon after the rain

408
00:24:21,740 --> 00:24:27,120
Walking while looking back,
pulled along by the gacha clatter

409
00:24:28,280 --> 00:24:34,280
That strange feeling I had back then

410
00:24:35,460 --> 00:24:39,540
So on the tiles of the arcade street

411
00:24:39,540 --> 00:24:45,300
I tried walking only on the black ones

412
00:24:47,800 --> 00:24:53,580
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten

413
00:24:54,500 --> 00:24:57,580
Not the politicians with
their self-important faces

414
00:24:57,580 --> 00:25:00,920
Nor the aunties with blue eyeshadow

415
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:06,520
Turn that corner, come on

416
00:25:07,460 --> 00:25:11,740
You can meet everyone, everyone

417
00:25:12,260 --> 00:25:19,680
Over there, there are walls,
well, surely there are walls

418
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:24,880
Everyone, come along to our town

419
00:25:25,700 --> 00:25:26,460
Thank you

420
00:25:30,480 --> 00:25:30,840
Thank you

421
00:25:31,800 --> 00:25:35,180
Why is this Kusaya natto ramen,
blue cheese flavor,

422
00:25:35,180 --> 00:25:37,200
ranked number one on a ranking show?

423
00:25:37,200 --> 00:25:40,340
Can you even trust rankings
someone else decided?

424
00:25:40,340 --> 00:25:43,960
In that case,
I'll decide the real ranking myself.

425
00:25:44,380 --> 00:25:47,700
Look forward to the next
decided ranking, okay?

426
00:25:56,460 --> 00:25:59,220
Come along to our town

427
00:26:00,160 --> 00:26:00,800
Thank you

